# Travel Forms Pilot — workspace startup file (EXAMPLE)

Copy this file to the **root of the folder you connect** — the one that contains
both `travel-forms-pilot/` and your trip folders — and name it `CLAUDE.md`:

```bash
cp travel-forms-pilot/CLAUDE.md.example ./CLAUDE.md
```

Then delete this header and adjust the paths below to match your layout.

**When this file is read.** Claude Code (CLI) and Cowork tasks running *on your
computer* read a `CLAUDE.md` at the root of the working folder automatically.
Cowork tasks running *in the cloud* reach your disk over the device bridge and do
**not** load it automatically — installing `SKILL.md` as a skill is what makes
the pilot work in that mode. See the README, "Using with Claude". Keeping this
file is still worth it: it costs nothing and it is what makes `claude` in this
folder behave correctly.

---

# Travel Forms Pilot — read this first, every session

At the start of every session, read these files in order before answering
anything:

1. `STATUS.md` — current state, open tasks, what happened last session.
   *(Optional: create one if you like a running log; the pilot works without it.)*
2. `travel-forms-pilot/SKILL.md` — full agent behaviour and rules.
3. `travel-forms-pilot/prompts/00_pilot.md` — base behaviour in detail.
4. `travel-forms-pilot/learnings.md` — accumulated trip-specific rules.
5. `personal/identity.yaml` — personal master data (name, personnel number,
   cost centre, bonus programmes). Not in git.

Only after reading those should you respond to the user's first message.

## Where things live

```
TRAVEL-FORMS/                        ← connect THIS folder
├── CLAUDE.md                        ← you are here
├── STATUS.md                        ← optional running log
├── personal/                        ← NOT in git
│   ├── identity.yaml                ← personal master data
│   └── bonus_points.md              ← running BahnBonus + Miles & More balance
├── travel-forms-pilot/              ← the pilot repo (git)
│   ├── SKILL.md
│   ├── prompts/                     ← 00_pilot, 40_backlog, 50_dashboard, 60_calendar, 70_closing
│   ├── learnings.md
│   ├── scripts/                     ← bootstrap_trip, fill_application, fill_expense, dashboard, …
│   ├── templates/                   ← trip.md.tmpl, blank DOCX forms
│   ├── config/                      ← mpi-susmat.yaml (institutional constants)
│   └── docs/                        ← formular_mechanik.md (field index tables)
├── dashboard.html                   ← regenerated by scripts/dashboard.py
│
├── 20260901_Cargese_MecaNano-school/   ← trip folders live HERE,
├── 202609_ISAM5_Tokyo/                 ←   not inside travel-forms-pilot/
└── …
```

## Key rules

- **Never hand-edit XML in the DOCX templates.** Always go through the scripts:
  - `scripts/bootstrap_trip.py <trip-folder>` — scaffold subfolders + `trip.md`
  - `scripts/fill_application.py --config <yaml> --output-dir <dir>` — Dienstreiseantrag
  - `scripts/fill_expense.py --config <yaml> --output-dir <dir>` — Reiseabrechnung
  - `scripts/dashboard.py <trips-root>` — regenerate `dashboard.html`
- **Calendar work goes through the `calmcp` MCP server**, not through a script —
  `cm_absence` for the all-day absence block, `ic_travel` for travel legs and
  hotels. Every write is a dry-run until confirmed; `cm_absence` also needs
  `confirm_foreign`. See `travel-forms-pilot/prompts/60_calendar.md`.
- **Trip folders are created here, never inside `travel-forms-pilot/`.** If a
  named trip folder doesn't exist yet, ask where to put it.
